## 2. Iterations (B5 variants; 5 or 4 worlds per class of base 7000000; counts of the arm's OWN answers)
# iteration A: anytime ladder to the full cap + registered probes + support test (5/class, budget 8/12/24 control)
control b8:  B4 correct 23/80 | B5 16 | B5 without ladder 11 | B5 ladder only (no registration) 23
control b12: B4 47/80        | B5 40 | B5 without ladder 37 | B5 ladder only 47
control b24: B4 79/80        | B5 73 | B5 without ladder 74 | B5 ladder only 78
=> the ladder alone recovers NOTHING (the engine does not claim at a smaller cap: its claim needs the
   replicates it spends); registration as first built cost 5-7 identifications (support tests ran after
   the null probes had used the budget). Fixes: support test before null probes; gate-led claim.
